  data: {
    LLM: "In the early phases, play defensively to erase your strokes as quickly as possible and drop out before the game becomes 'sharp'.\n\nCounting to 66: Always track the point value of the tricks you have taken. Reaching 66 allows you to 'close' the deck and stop opponents from drawing better cards.\n\nSlate Management: Observe how many strokes opponents have left. If a player is on their last stroke, do not feed them high-point cards (Aces/Tens).",
    Player: "In the early phases, play defensively to erase your strokes as quickly as possible and drop out before the game becomes 'sharp'.\n\nCounting to 66: Always track the point value of the tricks you have taken. Reaching 66 allows you to 'close' the deck and stop opponents from drawing better cards.\n\nSlate Management: Observe how many strokes opponents have left. If a player is on their last stroke, do not feed them high-point cards (Aces/Tens).",
